$$------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ DP600 single-element uniaxial tension  --  Altair OptiStruct
$$
$$   units : mm - N - tonne - s   (stress MPa, density 7.85-9)
$$   model : 1 x 1 x 1 mm CHEXA, 1/8 symmetry, x-face pulled to u = 0.5 mm
$$   check : sigma_x ~= 700.3 MPa at the end (see README.md)
$$
$$   run   : optistruct dp600-1elem-optistruct.fem
$$
$$   TABLES1 here is stress vs TOTAL strain (MATS1 TYPSTRN left blank = 0).
$$   With TYPSTRN = 0 the first point is the origin and the SECOND point must be
$$   the yield point, so that those two points reproduce the elastic slope of
$$   MAT1: 350 / 210000 = 0.00167.  Set TYPSTRN = 1 and the same table would be
$$   read as stress vs PLASTIC strain -- a different curve entirely.
$$------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ I/O Options
SCREEN,OUT
OUTPUT,H3D
DISPLACEMENT(H3D) = ALL
STRESS(H3D)       = ALL
STRAIN(H3D)       = ALL
SPCFORCE(H3D)     = ALL
$$
$$ Subcase Information
SUBCASE 1
  LABEL    = pull x face to 0.5 mm
  ANALYSIS = NLSTAT
  SPC      = 1
  LOAD     = 2
  NLPARM   = 10
$$
BEGIN BULK
$
$ ANALYSIS=NLSTAT on its own is SMALL displacement nonlinear.  Large strain
$ elasto-plasticity with MATS1 needs the large displacement solution, and
$ Altair's own material says LGDISP "needs to be used together with hash
$ assembly option (PARAM,HASHASSM,YES)" -- both are set here.
$ In large displacement analysis the curve is read as TRUE stress / TRUE strain.
PARAM,LGDISP,1
PARAM,HASHASSM,YES
$
$       ID      NINC    DT      KMETHOD KSTEP   MAXITER CONV
NLPARM  10      50              AUTO    5       25      UPW
$
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ MESH
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GRID    1               0.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    2               1.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    3               1.0     1.0     0.0
GRID    4               0.0     1.0     0.0
GRID    5               0.0     0.0     1.0
GRID    6               1.0     0.0     1.0
GRID    7               1.0     1.0     1.0
GRID    8               0.0     1.0     1.0
$
CHEXA   1       1       1       2       3       4       5       6
+       7       8
$
PSOLID  1       1       0
$
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ MATERIAL   -- MATS1 supplements the MAT1 with the same MID; both are needed
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MAT1    1       210000.         0.3     7.85-9
$
$       MID     TID     TYPE    H       YF      HR      LIMIT1  LIMIT2
MATS1   1       200     PLASTIC         1       1       350.0
$
$ stress vs TOTAL strain.  8-character fields, so the values butt up against
$ each other -- that is normal fixed format, not a typo.  Pairs are:
$   (0, 0) (.0016667, 350) (.0221667, 455) (.1026667, 560)
$   (.4033333, 700) (1.003761, 790)
$ The second point reproduces the elastic slope of MAT1: 350/.0016667 = 210000.
TABLES1 200
+       .0000000.0000000.0016667350.0000.0221667455.0000.1026667560.0000
+       .4033333700.00001.003761790.0000
+       ENDT
$
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
$$ BOUNDARY CONDITIONS   (1/8 symmetry + enforced displacement)
$$   The pulled DOF must be in the SPC set; SPCD supplies its value and the
$$   subcase must select that SPCD set through LOAD.
$$-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SPC1    1       1       1       4       5       8
SPC1    1       2       1       2       5       6
SPC1    1       3       1       2       3       4
SPC1    1       1       2       3       6       7
$
SPCD    2       2       1       0.5     3       1       0.5
SPCD    2       6       1       0.5     7       1       0.5
$
ENDDATA
